  "title": "Make help-sync run the full sync and fix its keyword verification",
  "description": "- Invoking the help-sync skill now means one complete `sync --authorize-production` run to\n  verified publication on both endpoints. It no longer downgrades to audit/plan, asks before\n  publishing, or holds help back because production does not yet run the code it documents\n  (skill, agent metadata, AGENTS.md).\n- The representative lookup in `verify_endpoint()` matched stored keywords with `BINARY`, but\n  catalog keywords are normalized to upper case while most stored rows keep their authored case.\n  Every sync stopped once the sampled middle entry (`mastermind`, stored as `Mastermind`) was\n  mixed case. It now matches case-insensitively, like the game's lookup.\n\nValidation: help-sync suite with `LUMINARI_HELP_SYNC_INTEGRATION=1` (38 tests; the new\n`test_verify_accepts_stored_keywords_in_authored_case` fails without the fix); local\n`quality-format-check` and `hygiene-hygiene` jobs.",
